  "query_preview": "../Tuesday through Friday/...The current expectation \nremains for main frontal precipitation to push through on Tuesday \nwith a mean 24 hour rainfall accumulation of 0.20\u201d mainly at \nhigher elevations, with 0.10\u201d more likely over locations at sea \nlevel. Intermittent easterly waves may provide additional light \nrain periodically through the week for the central to northern \nregions, though probabilities decrease as the surface high \npressure over the panhandle strengthens from Wednesday onward. As \nthe midweek system departs, clearing skies across the central and \nsouthern panhandle will drive a warming trend, supported by 850mb \ntemperature anomalies reaching approximately 4 to 5 deg C above \nseasonal norms. The Extreme Forecast Index (EFI) highlights this \ntrend beginning Wednesday and continuing through Friday, \nparticularly at higher elevations and broadly across the panhandle\nas the upper level ridge settles in. High temperatures are likely\nto reach the low to mid 70s, with some inland and southern areas \npotentially nearing heat advisory thresholds (80 deg F) as skies \nclear toward the weekend. Finally, winds are expected to remain \nlight throughout the period, though diurnal sea breezes will \nlikely increase in response to warmer surface temperatures and a \nshift to weak WNW onshore flow by Friday.",
